module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.CanonicalSectionsInjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleWire.UnitStalk

/-!
# Towards surjectivity of the canonical map to sections on an open complement

Let `X` be a scheme, let `I` be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals on `X` given by its
affine-local ideal data, and let `F` be an `𝒪_X`-module. Writing `U` for the open complement
`X \ V(I)`, the canonical map
`colim_n Hom(I ^ n • 𝒪_X, F) ⟶ Γ(F, U)`
of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections` is injective under the hypotheses of Stacks
tag 01PQ; this file collects what is needed for the complementary statement, that it is
surjective, which is the remaining content of Stacks tag 01YB.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_apply`: the value of the canonical map on the
  class of a representative is the evaluation of that representative on the unit section over
  the whole complement.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_surjective_iff`: surjectivity of the canonical
  map is exactly the solvability, for every section over the complement, of the extension
  problem of finding a morphism out of some `I ^ n • 𝒪_X` evaluating to it.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.basicOpen_le_idealComplement`: the basic open of an element of the
  ideal on an affine chart is disjoint from `V(I)`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.affine_inf_idealComplement_eq_iSup_basicOpen`: on an affine chart the
  complement of `V(I)` is the union of the basic opens of the elements of the ideal there.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_eq_restrict`: a section of a quasi-coherent module
  over a basic open of an affine open extends to the affine open after multiplication by a power
  of the defining element.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_restrict_eq_zero`: a section over an affine
  open which restricts to zero on a basic open is annihilated by a power of the defining element.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_compatible_family`: the normal form of the local data attached
  to a section over the complement by a finite family of elements of the ideal on an affine
  chart — one common exponent `k`, local extensions `m i` of `(a i) ^ k · s`, and the *exact*
  relations `(a j) ^ k • m i = (a i) ^ k • m j`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.affine_inf_idealComplement_eq_iSup_basicOpen_of_span`: if the ideal on
  an affine chart is generated by a family `a`, the chart meets the complement of `V(I)` in the
  union of the basic opens of the `a i`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine`: on an affine chart on which the
  ideal is generated by a finite family `a`, a section of a quasi-coherent module over
  `X \ V(I)` becomes, after multiplication by `(a i) ^ k` for one exponent `k` serving every
  `i`, the restriction of a section over the whole chart. This is the local form of the
  surjectivity statement of Stacks tag 01YB.

## Implementation notes

Surjectivity is not proved here. What `exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine` leaves open is the
passage from the local extensions to a morphism `I ^ n • 𝒪_X ⟶ F`: the exponent `k` it produces
depends on the chart, and turning the extensions into a morphism out of an ideal power is the
affine case of the argument, Stacks tag 01PM, which needs the quotient of `F` by the sections
annihilated by `I ^ n` before the extensions are well defined on `I ^ n`. The proof of Tag 01YB
then removes that quotient using the Artin–Rees lemma — available here as
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ideal_pow_smul_inf_eq` — and the fact that a quasi-coherent module on
a Noetherian scheme is the filtered union of its coherent submodules, whose colimit half is not
available here.

Sections of `F` are written `Γ(F, V)` with its `Γ(X, V)`-module structure, and restriction is
`F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op`; the scalar appearing after restriction is the restriction of
the scalar, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.map_smul`. The localization statements
are the quasi-coherence of `F` in the form
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange.isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ`, whose module
structure on the sections over a basic open is `QuasicoherentBaseChange.moduleOfLE`, obtained by
restricting scalars along the restriction map of the structure sheaf; that structure agrees with
the native one after applying the restriction map to the scalar, which is why the statements
below carry the restricted scalar explicitly rather than a `letI`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

open Stacks.Ample (unitModule)

noncomputable section

/-! ### The canonical map evaluated on a representative -/

/-- The value of the canonical map on the class of a representative `φ` is the evaluation of `φ`
on the unit section of `I ^ n • 𝒪_X` over the whole complement of `V(I)`.

This is the characterising property of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections` taken on
the complement itself, where the restriction map is the identity. -/
public lemma canonicalMapToSections_apply {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) (n : ℕ)
    (φ : (idealPowerSystem I (unitModule X)).obj (op n) ⟶ F) :
    (canonicalMapToSections I F).1 (colimit.ι (idealPowerHom I (unitModule X) F) n φ) =
      (φ.val.app (op (idealComplement I))).hom
        (complementUnitLift I n (idealComplement I) le_rfl) := by
  have h := (canonicalMapToSections I F).property n φ (idealComplement I) le_rfl
    (complementUnitLift I n (idealComplement I) le_rfl)
    (complementUnitLift_spec I n (idealComplement I) le_rfl)
  rwa [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE (le_refl (idealComplement I))).op
    (𝟙 (op (idealComplement I))), CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id] at h

/-- Surjectivity of the canonical map is the solvability of the extension problem: every section
of `F` over `X \ V(I)` is the evaluation, on the unit section, of some morphism
`I ^ n • 𝒪_X ⟶ F`.

This is the form in which the surjectivity half of Stacks tag 01YB is proved: one produces the
morphism, rather than an element of the colimit. -/
public lemma canonicalMapToSections_surjective_iff {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) :
    Function.Surjective (canonicalMapToSections I F).1 ↔
      ∀ s : Γ(F, idealComplement I), ∃ (n : ℕ)
        (φ : (idealPowerSystem I (unitModule X)).obj (op n) ⟶ F),
          (φ.val.app (op (idealComplement I))).hom
            (complementUnitLift I n (idealComplement I) le_rfl) = s := by
  refine ⟨fun h s => ?_, fun h s => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h s
    obtain ⟨n, φ, rfl⟩ := Types.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit
      (colimit.isColimit (idealPowerHom I (unitModule X) F)) x
    exact ⟨n, φ, (canonicalMapToSections_apply I F n φ).symm.trans hx⟩
  · obtain ⟨n, φ, hφ⟩ := h s
    exact ⟨colimit.ι (idealPowerHom I (unitModule X) F) n φ,
      (canonicalMapToSections_apply I F n φ).trans hφ⟩

/-! ### The complement of `V(I)` on an affine chart -/

/-- The basic open of an element of the ideal on an affine chart is disjoint from the support of
the ideal sheaf. -/
public lemma basicOpen_le_idealComplement {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) {a : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (ha : a ∈ I.ideal U) :
    X.basicOpen a ≤ idealComplement I := by
  intro y hy
  have hyU : y ∈ (U : X.Opens) := X.basicOpen_le a hy
  have hyS : y ∈ I.support → False := by
    intro hyS
    have hyZ : y ∈ X.zeroLocus (U := (U : X.Opens)) (I.ideal U) :=
      (I.mem_support_iff_of_mem hyU).mp hyS
    exact (Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff X (I.ideal U : Set Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) y).mp hyZ a ha hy
  simpa [idealComplement] using hyS

/-- A point of an affine chart lies away from `V(I)` exactly when some element of the ideal on
that chart does not vanish at it. -/
public lemma exists_mem_ideal_mem_basicOpen {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) {y : X} (hyU : y ∈ (U : X.Opens)) (hy : y ∈ idealComplement I) :
    ∃ a ∈ I.ideal U, y ∈ X.basicOpen a := by
  have hyS : y ∉ I.support := by simpa [idealComplement] using hy
  have hyZ : y ∉ X.zeroLocus (U := (U : X.Opens)) (I.ideal U) := fun h =>
    hyS ((I.mem_support_iff_of_mem hyU).mpr h)
  rw [Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff] at hyZ
  simpa using hyZ

/-- On an affine chart the complement of `V(I)` is the union of the basic opens of the elements
of the ideal there. -/
public lemma affine_inf_idealComplement_eq_iSup_basicOpen {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) :
    (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I =
      ⨆ a : I.ideal U, X.basicOpen (a : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun y hy => ?_)
    (iSup_le fun a => le_inf (X.basicOpen_le _) (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U a.property))
  obtain ⟨a, ha, hya⟩ := exists_mem_ideal_mem_basicOpen I U hy.1 hy.2
  exact TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, hya⟩

/-- The restriction map to a basic open of an affine open is a localization at the powers of the
defining element. -/
private theorem isLocalizedModule_away_restrictₗ {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    letI := moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le a)
    IsLocalizedModule.Away a (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le a)) :=
  isLocalizedModule_restrictₗ F hU a rfl (X.basicOpen_le a)

/-- Elements of a family generating the ideal on a chart lie in the ideal. -/
private theorem mem_ideal_of_span {X : Scheme.{u}} {I : X.IdealSheafData} {U : X.affineOpens}
    {ι : Type*} {a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (hspan : I.ideal U = Ideal.span (Set.range a))
    (i : ι) : a i ∈ I.ideal U :=
  hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩

/-! ### Local extension of sections of a quasi-coherent module -/

/-- A section of a quasi-coherent module over a basic open `X_a` of an affine open `U` becomes
the restriction of a section over `U` after multiplication by a power of `a`.

The restriction map `Γ(F, U) → Γ(F, X_a)` is a localization at the powers of `a`, so this is the
surjectivity statement for a localization. -/
public lemma exists_pow_smul_eq_restrict {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (a : Γ(X, U)) (s : Γ(F, X.basicOpen a)) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (m : Γ(F, U)),
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op m =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op a) ^ k • s := by
  let := moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le a)
  have hloc := isLocalizedModule_away_restrictₗ F hU a
  obtain ⟨⟨m, t⟩, ht⟩ :=
    IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers a) (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le a)) s
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := (Submonoid.mem_powers_iff t.1 a).mp t.2
  refine ⟨k, m, ?_⟩
  have h1 : (a ^ k) • s = restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le a) m := by rwa [hk]
  have h2 : (a ^ k) • s =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op a) ^ k • s := by
    change (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op (a ^ k)) • s = _
    rw [map_pow]
  exact h1.symm.trans h2

/-- A section of a quasi-coherent module over an affine open which restricts to zero on the basic
open of `a` is annihilated by a power of `a`.

The restriction map is a localization at the powers of `a`, so this is the description of its
kernel. -/
public lemma exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_restrict_eq_zero {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (a : Γ(X, U)) (x : Γ(F, U))
    (hx : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le a)).op x = 0) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, a ^ N • x = 0 := by
  let := moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le a)
  have hloc := isLocalizedModule_away_restrictₗ F hU a
  have hx' : restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le a) x = 0 := hx
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ :=
    (IsLocalizedModule.eq_zero_iff (Submonoid.powers a)
      (f := restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le a))).mp hx'
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := (Submonoid.mem_powers_iff t.1 a).mp t.2
  exact ⟨N, by rw [hN]; exact ht⟩

/-! ### Transitivity of restriction -/

/-- Restricting sections of an `𝒪_X`-module along two nested inclusions of opens is restricting
along the composite. -/
public lemma map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE {X : Scheme.{u}} (M : X.Modules) {V W Y : X.Opens}
    (h₁ : W ≤ V) (h₂ : Y ≤ W) (x : Γ(M, V)) :
    M.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op x) =
      M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h₂.trans h₁)).op x := by
  rw [← homOfLE_comp h₂ h₁, op_comp, M.presheaf.map_comp_apply]

/-- Restricting sections of the structure sheaf along two nested inclusions of opens is
restricting along the composite. -/
public lemma structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE {X : Scheme.{u}} {V W Y : X.Opens}
    (h₁ : W ≤ V) (h₂ : Y ≤ W) (x : Γ(X, V)) :
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op x) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h₂.trans h₁)).op x := by
  rw [← homOfLE_comp h₂ h₁, op_comp, X.presheaf.map_comp_apply]

/-! ### The local data attached to a section over the complement -/

/-- A finite family of elements of the ideal on an affine chart gives, for a section `s` of a
quasi-coherent module over the complement of `V(I)`, local extensions of `(a i) ^ k · s` over the
chart with one exponent `k` serving every member of the family.

This is `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_eq_restrict` applied to each `a i` separately,
followed by raising every exponent to their supremum. -/
public lemma exists_uniform_pow_smul_eq_restrict {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (U : X.affineOpens)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) (ha : ∀ i, a i ∈ I.ideal U)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (m : ι → Γ(F, (U : X.Opens))), ∀ i,
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i))).op (m i) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i))).op (a i)) ^ k •
          F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (ha i))).op s := by
  classical
  have : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  choose k m hm using fun i =>
    exists_pow_smul_eq_restrict F U.2 (a i)
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (ha i))).op s)
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.sup k, fun i => a i ^ (Finset.univ.sup k - k i) • m i, fun i => ?_⟩
  rw [F.map_smul, hm i, map_pow, smul_smul, ← pow_add,
    Nat.sub_add_cancel (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ i))]

/-- The normal form of the local data attached to a section over the complement of `V(I)` by a
finite family `a` of elements of the ideal on an affine chart `U`: one exponent `k`, sections
`m i` over `U` restricting on `X_{a i}` to `(a i) ^ k · s`, and the *exact* relations
`(a j) ^ k • m i = (a i) ^ k • m j` in `Γ(F, U)`.

The relations hold only after multiplication by a further power of the ideal: on `X_{a i a j}`
the two sections `(a j) ^ k • m i` and `(a i) ^ k • m j` agree, because both restrict to
`(a i a j) ^ k · s`, and quasi-coherence turns that into annihilation of their difference by a
power of `a i a j`; the family is then renormalised by that power.

These are exactly the relations that the affine case of the argument, Stacks tag 01PM, feeds
into the construction of a morphism out of an ideal power. -/
public lemma exists_compatible_family {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (U : X.affineOpens)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) (ha : ∀ i, a i ∈ I.ideal U)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (m : ι → Γ(F, (U : X.Opens))),
      (∀ i, F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i))).op (m i) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i))).op (a i)) ^ k •
          F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (ha i))).op s) ∧
      ∀ i j, a j ^ k • m i = a i ^ k • m j := by
  classical
  have : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  obtain ⟨k₀, m, hm⟩ := exists_uniform_pow_smul_eq_restrict I F U a ha s
  have hrestrict : ∀ (i : ι) (W : X.Opens) (hW : W ≤ X.basicOpen (a i)),
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hW.trans (X.basicOpen_le (a i)))).op (m i) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hW.trans (X.basicOpen_le (a i)))).op (a i)) ^ k₀ •
          F.presheaf.map
            (homOfLE (hW.trans (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (ha i)))).op s := by
    intro i W hW
    rw [← map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (a i)) hW (m i), hm i, F.map_smul,
      map_pow, structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  have hd : ∀ i j, F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i * a j))).op
      (a j ^ k₀ • m i - a i ^ k₀ • m j) = 0 := by
    intro i j
    have hi : X.basicOpen (a i * a j) ≤ X.basicOpen (a i) :=
      (X.basicOpen_mul (a i) (a j)).le.trans inf_le_left
    have hj : X.basicOpen (a i * a j) ≤ X.basicOpen (a j) :=
      (X.basicOpen_mul (a i) (a j)).le.trans inf_le_right
    rw [map_sub, F.map_smul, F.map_smul, map_pow, map_pow, sub_eq_zero,
      hrestrict i _ hi, hrestrict j _ hj]
    exact smul_comm _ _ _
  choose N hN using fun p : ι × ι =>
    exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_restrict_eq_zero F U.2 (a p.1 * a p.2)
      (a p.2 ^ k₀ • m p.1 - a p.1 ^ k₀ • m p.2) (hd p.1 p.2)
  obtain ⟨K, hK⟩ : ∃ K : ℕ, ∀ p : ι × ι, N p ≤ K :=
    ⟨Finset.univ.sup N, fun p => Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ p)⟩
  have hkill : ∀ i j, (a i * a j) ^ K • (a j ^ k₀ • m i - a i ^ k₀ • m j) = 0 := fun i j => by
    rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel (hK (i, j)), pow_add, mul_smul, hN (i, j), smul_zero]
  refine ⟨k₀ + K, fun i => a i ^ K • m i, fun i => ?_, fun i j => ?_⟩
  · rw [F.map_smul, hm i, map_pow, smul_smul, ← pow_add, Nat.add_comm K k₀]
  · have h := hkill i j
    rw [smul_sub, sub_eq_zero, smul_smul, smul_smul] at h
    rwa [smul_smul, smul_smul,
      show a j ^ (k₀ + K) * a i ^ K = (a i * a j) ^ K * a j ^ k₀ by ring,
      show a i ^ (k₀ + K) * a j ^ K = (a i * a j) ^ K * a i ^ k₀ by ring]

/-! ### Extension over an affine chart -/

/-- If the ideal on an affine chart is generated by a family `a`, then a point of the chart lies
away from `V(I)` exactly when some `a i` does not vanish at it. -/
public lemma exists_mem_basicOpen_of_span {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (U : X.affineOpens) {ι : Type*} (a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    (hspan : I.ideal U = Ideal.span (Set.range a))
    {y : X} (hyU : y ∈ (U : X.Opens)) (hy : y ∈ idealComplement I) :
    ∃ i, y ∈ X.basicOpen (a i) := by
  have hyS : y ∉ I.support := by simpa [idealComplement] using hy
  by_contra hno
  refine hyS ((I.mem_support_iff_of_mem hyU).mpr ?_)
  rw [hspan, Scheme.zeroLocus_span, Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff]
  rintro f ⟨i, rfl⟩ hf
  exact hno ⟨i, hf⟩

/-- If the ideal on an affine chart `U` is generated by a family `a`, then `U` meets the
complement of `V(I)` in the union of the basic opens `X_{a i}`. -/
public lemma affine_inf_idealComplement_eq_iSup_basicOpen_of_span {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens) {ι : Type*} (a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    (hspan : I.ideal U = Ideal.span (Set.range a)) :
    (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I = ⨆ i, X.basicOpen (a i) := by
  have hamem := mem_ideal_of_span hspan
  exact le_antisymm (fun y hy => TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2
      (exists_mem_basicOpen_of_span I U a hspan hy.1 hy.2))
    (iSup_le fun i => le_inf (X.basicOpen_le _) (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (hamem i)))

/-- **A section away from `V(I)` extends over an affine chart after multiplication by a power of
the ideal.** Let `F` be quasi-coherent, let `U` be an affine open on which the ideal is generated
by a finite family `a`, and let `s` be a section of `F` over `X \ V(I)`. Then there is an
exponent `k` and, for each `i`, a section `m i` of `F` over `U` whose restriction to
`U ∖ V(I)` is `(a i) ^ k · s`.

This is the local form of the surjectivity statement of Stacks tag 01YB. The sections `m i` come
from the compatible family of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_compatible_family`, which produces
them only over the basic opens `X_{a i}`; the point of this lemma is that the relations
`(a j) ^ k • m i = (a i) ^ k • m j` force `m i` to agree with `(a i) ^ k · s` over all of
`U ∖ V(I)`, because `a j` acts invertibly on the sections over `X_{a j}` and those basic opens
cover `U ∖ V(I)`. -/
public lemma exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine {X : Scheme.{u}} (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (U : X.affineOpens)
    {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (a : ι → Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    (hspan : I.ideal U = Ideal.span (Set.range a))
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ (k : ℕ) (m : ι → Γ(F, (U : X.Opens))), ∀ i,
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left :
          (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I ≤ (U : X.Opens))).op (m i) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left :
            (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I ≤ (U : X.Opens))).op (a i)) ^ k •
          F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_right :
            (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I ≤ idealComplement I)).op s := by
  classical
  have hamem := mem_ideal_of_span hspan
  obtain ⟨k, m, hm, hrel⟩ := exists_compatible_family I F U a hamem s
  refine ⟨k, m, fun i => ?_⟩
  apply TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext F.isSheaf
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨j, hyj⟩ := exists_mem_basicOpen_of_span I U a hspan hy.1 hy.2
  refine ⟨X.basicOpen (a j),
    le_inf (X.basicOpen_le _) (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (hamem j)), hyj, ?_⟩
  have hcan : ∀ x y : Γ(F, X.basicOpen (a j)),
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a j))).op (a j)) ^ k • x =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a j))).op (a j)) ^ k • y → x = y := by
    intro x y hxy
    let := moduleOfLE F (X.basicOpen_le (a j))
    have hloc := isLocalizedModule_away_restrictₗ F U.2 (a j)
    refine (IsLocalizedModule.smul_inj (restrictₗ F (X.basicOpen_le (a j)))
      (⟨a j ^ k, (Submonoid.mem_powers_iff _ _).mpr ⟨k, rfl⟩⟩ : Submonoid.powers (a j))
      x y).mp ?_
    change (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a j))).op (a j ^ k)) • x =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a j))).op (a j ^ k)) • y
    rwa [map_pow]
  have h1 := congrArg (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a j))).op) (hrel i j)
  rw [F.map_smul, F.map_smul, map_pow, map_pow, hm j] at h1
  rw [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, F.map_smul, map_pow,
    structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  refine hcan _ _ ?_
  rw [h1]
  exact smul_comm _ _ _

end

end Stacks.LocalCohomology

